  "all_ingredients_flat": "millet, quinoa, oat flour, yellow peas, greens, onion, tomatoes, sweet potatoes, ginger, garlic, green chillies, spices of your choice, misc spices",
  "instructions": "PATTICE: Mix cooked millet (any millet; can be made with quinoa too), boiled sweet potatoes, diced onion, ginger, green chillies, spices of your choice. Make small balls (mix more millet or oat flour if the dough is too soft). Flatten the ball on a hot pan. Cook both sides. RAGDA: Stir fried onion, garlic, ginger (water saut\u00e9ed). Add overnight soaked yellow peas. Add tomatoes (optional) and spices of your choice. Add enough water to cover the peas. Cook till peas are firm. Give it a good stir. Add greens while still hot & cover until ready to serve.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "boil",
    "pan-fry",
    "saute"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Serve hot with greens.",
  "notes": "This recipe consists of two main components: Pattice and Ragda. For Pattice, millet can be substituted with quinoa, and oat flour can be added if the dough is too soft. For Ragda, tomatoes are optional.",
